            <ArticleTitle>Conduct of multisite clinical studies by professional organizations.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="ISSUES AND PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Professional organizations are embracing collaborative multisite research and research utilization projects. This report describes the strategies undertaken and lessons learned from SPN's first multisite study.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Infrastructure concerns (e.g., vision, communication, dissemination of results, resources, and human rights protections) and methodological issues specific to multisite research must be addressed to ensure a successful study.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="PRACTICE IMPLICATIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Multisite studies are an effective mechanism for more rapidly advancing nursing theory and evidence-based nursing practice.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
